OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G1/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe start of 1975 brought significant
OL,7,Fcuts to BBC services to save money.
OL,9,FAfternoon TV on BBC One went, BBC Two's
OL,10,Fweekend hours were curtailed and both
OL,11,Fnetworks closed by 11.30pm on
OL,12,Fweeknights.
OL,14,FThese were painful cuts which reduced
OL,15,Fchoice for viewers ` in particular
OL,16,Fthose at home in the afternoon
OL,17,Fincluding the housebound.
OL,19,FOne other cut took effect a few weeks
OL,20,Flater on 20th January 1975.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FTrade test transmissions on BBC Two
OL,7,Fwere drastically curtailed.
OL,9,FUp until then, BBC Two transmitters had
OL,10,Fpumped out up to 10 hours of the test
OL,11,Fcard every day ` generally only
OL,12,Finterrupted for Play School at 11am.
OL,14,FUntil August 1973, the trade test
OL,15,Ftransmissions also included colour
OL,16,Ffilms to provide moving images to
OL,17,Fdemonstrate sets.
OL,19,FGoodness knows what the Carbon
OL,20,Ffootprint was, to use the language of
OL,21,Ftoday.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13403
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn January 1975 the axe fell. Generally
OL,7,FBBC Two transmitters were only on the
OL,8,Fair between 10.30am and 11.30am and
OL,9,Ffrom 4pm until shortly after the final
OL,10,Fprogramme of the day.
OL,12,FThe cuts were justified by the need to
OL,13,Fsave both money and fuel.
OL,15,FAt the time, the corporation would have
OL,16,Fbeen billed for its electricity use
OL,17,Fdirectly in the same way as any other
OL,18,Fbusiness customer.
OL,20,FWhile the draconian power restrictions
OL,21,Fof early 1974 had gone, there were
OL,22,Fstill calls to save fuel.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13404
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FMost of Britain's electricity came from
OL,7,Fcoal and imported oil ` North Sea oil
OL,8,Fwas still to come on tap. Cutting the
OL,9,Fuse of power helped to reduce the use
OL,10,Fof oil for electricity generation.
OL,12,FIt's hard to argue against the logic of
OL,13,Fthis cut. Amongst the wider public,
OL,14,Fonly diehard fans of BBC Two's test
OL,15,Fcard music would have been
OL,16,Fdisappointed.
OL,18,FBut there is no doubt that this cut
OL,19,Fcaused significant inconvenience to the
OL,20,Ftrade.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13405
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe lack of a BBC Two signal for much
OL,7,Fof the daytime, made it harder to
OL,8,Finstall sets and aerials.
OL,10,FAn editorial in the magazine Television
OL,11,Fin April 1975 highlighted these
OL,12,Fconcerns.
OL,14,FTelevision, originally Practical
OL,15,FTelevision, was a useful magazine with
OL,16,Fgood advice for service engineers and
OL,17,FDX enthusiasts.
OL,19,FThe basic concerns were justified but I
OL,20,Fcannot help but think the writer went
OL,21,Fslightly over the score.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13406
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FFirst of all ` would the loss of the
OL,7,FBBC Two test card really cause massive
OL,8,Fproblems and lead to more badly
OL,9,Fadjusted sets?
OL,11,FFundamental adjustments to set up
OL,12,Ftelevisions ` like convergence checks
OL,13,Fand balancing the colour guns ` should
OL,14,Fhave been done in the workshop, not a
OL,15,Fhome. Many of these checks should have
OL,16,Fbeen done with pattern generators.
OL,18,FWhen a set was installed in the
OL,19,Fviewer's home, it should only have been
OL,20,Fnecessary to tune it in and adjust the
OL,21,Fnormal controls like the brightness and
OL,22,Fcontrast.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13407
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe test card was basically diagnostic
OL,7,F` it showed up faults and allowed for
OL,8,Fadjustments.
OL,10,FThe loss of the test card on BBC Two
OL,11,Fwas, of course, partly balanced out by
OL,12,Fits increased use on BBC One in the
OL,13,Fafternoon after the programme cuts.
OL,15,FThe suggestion that there would often
OL,16,Fbe no colour signal to show the viewer
OL,17,Fseems a strange one.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13408
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G8/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FBy 1975, roughly half of BBC Schools
OL,7,Fprogrammes were in colour ` including
OL,8,Fall new ones. ITV meanwhile ran a full
OL,9,Fschedule from noon ` nothing was in
OL,10,Fblack and white except for the odd
OL,11,Ffilm.
OL,13,FA point about the colour quality of
OL,14,Fsome programmes is highly dubious.
OL,15,FSchools and daytime programmes operated
OL,16,Fto the same technical standards as the
OL,17,Frest of the schedule.
OL,19,FWhile the lack of any signal was
OL,20,Fcertainly inconvenient, UHF aerials
OL,21,Fgenerally gave equally good results on
OL,22,Fall channels.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13409
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G9/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn aerial properly adjusted for both
OL,7,FBBC One and ITV could be presumed to be
OL,8,Fset up properly for BBC Two. When
OL,9,FChannel 4 started, there was no need
OL,10,Ffor aerial adjustments except in the
OL,11,Ffew instances where Channel 4 was on an
OL,12,Funusual frequency.
OL,14,FStill, the move meant that many
OL,15,Fengineers would, understandably, only
OL,16,Fwant to install sets when a BBC Two
OL,17,Fsignal was available. But the secret
OL,18,Fwas to make the most of the available
OL,19,Ftime ` not to make grim predictions
OL,20,Fabout increased fuel use like the
OL,21,Fwriter does.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13410
SC,0010
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G10/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FAll a service engineer needed to do was
OL,7,Fbuy Radio Times to see when there'd be
OL,8,Fa BBC Two signal outside trade tests `
OL,9,Ffor instance because of midweek racing.
OL,11,FThe countdown number on the test card
OL,12,Fwas introduced in 1976 to make it
OL,13,Feasier for engineers to use the limited
OL,14,Ftime ` not to tell viewers when
OL,15,Fprogrammes would resume.
OL,17,FAll in all, it was a sensible economy
OL,18,Fcut. The sad thing is that the BBC's
OL,19,Ffinancial position and the state of the
OL,20,Fcountry made it necessary.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13411
SC,0011
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G11/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf took until 1983 to officially
OL,7,Freverse these cuts to BBC Two
OL,8,Ftransmission time. Shutdowns ended at
OL,9,Fthe same time as schools programmes
OL,10,Fmoved to Two.
OL,12,FIt's worth noting that things were
OL,13,Frelaxed slightly in 1980 when Ceefax
OL,14,FIn-Vision slots started ` usually in
OL,15,Fthe half hour up to 10.30am and 4pm.
OL,17,FIs any of this of relevance today or is
OL,18,Fit just anoraky nostalgia?
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13412
SC,0012
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G12/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FEvery organisation needs to think about
OL,7,Fits energy bill and carbon footprint `
OL,8,Ffor both economic and environmental
OL,9,Freasons.
OL,11,FThe idea of a major channel being off
OL,12,Fthe air during the daytime is
OL,13,Funthinkable while multiplexing means
OL,14,Fthat the transmitter would still be on
OL,15,Fair even if an individual channel was
OL,16,Fshut.
OL,18,FBut the Television article is a
OL,19,Freminder that it is possible to
OL,20,Foverstate the real challenges that
OL,21,Ftrying to save electricity can bring.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13413
SC,0013
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G13/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt painted a worst case scenario and
OL,7,Fpresented it as inevitable.
OL,9,FWith sensible planning and foresight,
OL,10,Fmany businesses and some domestic
OL,11,Fcustomers today could probably cut
OL,12,Ftheir power use and energy bills
OL,13,Fwithout too much hardship. Some already
OL,14,Fhave.
OL,16,FA growing proportion of the UK's
OL,17,Felectricity comes from renewables,
OL,18,Fnuclear power and "low carbon" sources
OL,19,Fsuch as biomass. Coal-fired power
OL,20,Fstations are a thing of the past.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13414
SC,0014
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F134A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G14/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FModern lights and TVs use far less
OL,7,Felectricity than their 1970s
OL,8,Fequivalents.
OL,10,FBut the mindful use of power can help
OL,11,Fsome people and businesses cut their
OL,12,Felectricity bills without causing the
OL,13,Fhardship of simply switching something
OL,14,Foff.
OL,23,APub: 18-Jan-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,135,120,200,300,0,100@
